<h1 id="literate-pages">Literate pages</h1>
<p>Links name symbols: <a href="docs/latest/std/list.html#fn-sort">std.list.sort</a>, <a href="docs/latest/std/list.html#fn-sort"><code>list.sort</code></a> through the hidden import
below, <a href="docs/latest/std/prelude.html#enum-option">Option</a> and <a href="docs/latest/std/prelude.html#enum-option">Some</a> from the prelude, and <a href="docs/latest/std/cursor.html#record-parsed"><code>Parsed.stop</code></a>, a field.
[std.list.merge_by] isn't exported, [nothing.here] isn't anything, and
[x, y] and [0] are only text. A definition wins: <a href="https://example.com/sort">sort</a>.</p>

<p>A block with <code>main</code> runs, and its output follows it:</p>
<pre><code class="language-checkers"><span class="kw">module</span> hello

<span class="kw">import</span> std.system (<span class="ty">System</span>, <span class="ty">ExitCode</span>)
<span class="kw">import</span> std.terminal

<span class="kw">export</span> <span class="kw">fn</span> main args sys -&gt; code : args~<span class="ty">List</span> <span class="ty">String</span>, sys~<span class="ty">System</span>, code~<span class="ty">ExitCode</span>
    terminal.print_line <span class="st">&quot;hello from a block&quot;</span> sys.term
    <span class="ty">Success</span>
</code></pre>
<pre class="output"><code>hello from a block
</code></pre>
<p>A block without a <code>module</code> line gets a hidden one; <code>#!</code> lines are compiled but
not shown:</p>
<pre><code class="language-checkers"><span class="kw">check</span> list.length [<span class="nu">1</span>, <span class="nu">2</span>, <span class="nu">3</span>] == <span class="nu">3</span>
</code></pre>
<pre class="fails" title="This code doesn't compile."><code class="language-checkers"><span class="kw">module</span> wrong

<span class="kw">fn</span> last xs -&gt; x : xs~<span class="ty">Bytes</span>, x~<span class="ty">U8</span>
    xs[len xs - <span class="nu">1</span>]
</code></pre>
<pre class="output"><code>error[E0450]: cannot prove that this `Nat` subtraction stays at or above zero
 --&gt; wrong.ck:4:8
  |
4 |     xs[len xs - 1]
  |        ^^^^^^^^^^ `-` on `Nat` needs the left side to be at least the right
  = note: counterexample: xs = b&quot;&quot;
  = help: check it first (`if a &gt;= b then a - b else …`), or use `Int`

wrong.ck: 1 error, 0 warnings
</code></pre>
<p>Warnings: a block that compiles though it shouldn't, one that fails with
another error than it says, one with an error, and one whose <code>main</code> fails.</p>
<pre class="fails" title="This code doesn't compile."><code class="language-checkers"><span class="kw">module</span> fine

<span class="kw">check</span> <span class="nu">1</span> + <span class="nu">1</span> == <span class="nu">2</span>
</code></pre>
<pre class="fails" title="This code doesn't compile."><code class="language-checkers"><span class="kw">module</span> other

<span class="kw">fn</span> f x -&gt; y : x~<span class="ty">Nat</span>, y~<span class="ty">Nat</span>
